#
# Counter-example for math:OrthogonalComplementShape: an orthogonal complement
# naming its ambient space and complement-semantics (so math:ComplementShape passes)
# but omitting math:definedByInnerProduct (sh:minCount 1). Referenced nodes are typed
# minimally so ONLY the missing-inner-product violation fires. Validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement).
# Bound by ex:ecOrthogonalComplementMissingInnerProduct.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:unqualifiedPerp a math:OrthogonalComplement ;
    math:orthogonalComplementOf ex:embeddedSub ;
    math:ambientSpace ex:complexSpace ;
    math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement .

ex:embeddedSub a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:complexSpace a math:MathematicalObject .
